  "note": "The nine retiring councillors were the only persons nominated (on Friday 5 January); Samuel Sterling, returning officer, declared them elected. The Belfast Gazette, 10 November 1922, records the Ministry of Home Affairs order that from 1923 the councillors be elected for the whole urban district as one area. James Fagan is the James Fegan (Labour) of 1920."
